  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through the argument line by line. Notice how Klavdiya teases Nina about Samsonov's growing popularity.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "klavdiya",
   "t": "Что, Нина, допрыгалась?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What, Nina, did you finally go too far?' The colloquial verb expresses reaching a bad outcome through reckless actions.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "klavdiya",
   "t": "Убежал твой Ваня к молодухе?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did your Vanya run off to a younger woman?' Preposition with dative indicates motion toward someone.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Кому он вообще нужен?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who even needs him anyway?' The short form adjective requires the dative case for the person in need.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "klavdiya",
   "t": "Если мэром станет, очередь выстроится!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If he becomes mayor, a whole line will form!' Conditional clause with instrumental case following the verb.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "klavdiya",
   "t": "Это официальный документ, между прочим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is an official document, by the way.' A common parenthetical phrase meaning incidentally or by the way.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Да вы же сами его хвалили!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why, you yourself were praising him!' Emphatic particles reinforce Nina's exasperation with her neighbour.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "klavdiya",
   "t": "Беги скорее с Ваней мириться!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Run quickly to make peace with Vanya!' Imperative verb with comparative adverb expressing urgent movement.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Вам надо, вы и миритесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If you need to, you go make peace.' Impersonal construction with dative pronoun expressing necessity.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Вечером придёт домой, как миленький.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Tonight he will come home, meek as a lamb.' An idiomatic phrase meaning obediently without protest.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "klavdiya",
   "t": "Ну, моё дело — только предупредить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, my job was only to warn you.' Fixed conversational idiom used when giving unsolicited advice.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Оставьте меня все в покое!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Leave me in peace, all of you!' Standard polite imperative phrase asking someone to leave you alone.",
